d to  almost any data type be it imaging mass  cytometry fluorescence or other  techniques  importantly multiplex phenotyping  invisiofarm integrates with existing  tools this means you can leverage the  power of our ai deep learning both for  cell detection but also as i briefly  mentioned identifying areas of interest  excluding artifacts or necrotic areas or  any other upstream tool that could  benefit from ai deep learning  and lastly the outputs are fully  customizable you really do get to decide  what questions you ask of your data  this could be quantitative measures as i  mentioned as summary statistics or  granular per cell data  density heat maps are very easy to  produce and to use  or are built built-in phenotyping plots  including disney's and neighborhood  analysis  i'd like to thank you for watching this  webinar today  i hope you've gained some valuable  insights into multiplexing and how the  vizio farm platform approaches these  sorts of analyses
 

